From 09914c032e8394044730366508e4ff88d239b052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:43:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Every slayer helmet colour, with OSRS's own art

The recolour shipped yesterday was built on a wrong assumption: that OSRS's
coloured slayer helmets are recolours. They are not. Red is model 42708, green
42705, black 42700 - separately authored meshes with recols=0, and different
vertex counts. Putting two recol pairs on the plain helmet only ever repainted
the mask and the strap, so "red" was the grey helmet with a red patch.

Fourteen colours now, each plain and imbued: black, green, red, purple,
turquoise, hydra, twisted, tztok, vampyric, tzkal, araxyte, hooded, oathplate,
radiant. 28 objs over 70 imported models, camera included - the cache does not
use one camera for all of them. Only twisted and radiant keep recol pairs,
because only those two are recolours in OSRS as well.

The imbued helmet got its own model too. OSRS obj 11865 is model 42702 where
the plain one is 42707, and it had been wearing the plain one since the imbue
round - asserted as correct by a check that was right about the black mask and
wrong about the helmet.

Twelve of the fourteen have no monster here and are built anyway, for ::give.
obtainable.py grew a section that names all 24 objs and reads the list from the
spec, so a colour that GAINS a source is reported as a disagreement rather than
silently excused. Black is one source block from real.

Everything in this round compares the config to the spec and the generator
writes one from the other, so the spec now records each colour's OSRS model id
and its converted vertex and face counts, and group 67 measures the shipped
files against them. Without that a colour pointed at the wrong art would have
been perfectly self-consistent.

poh_mutate.py now reports WHICH check went red, not just that something did.
That immediately found a weak one: the disassembly check compared sets of
colour names, so a helmet routed to the wrong disassembly with its imbued twin
left alone changed nothing it looked at. It names all 28 items now.

rs2check 0 ERROR, selftest PASS, poh_battery 67 groups ALL PASS, maxcape_battery
ALL PASS, four sims ALL PASS, obtainable.py clean. 14 mutations, all caught by
their own check. NOT compiled: npm is 403ing zod and yocto-queue again, so no
Engine-TS clone would install this session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dc7giZ7Qnh4qy1CYPTDrmH
